    {
      "type": "updated",
      "source": "wgmods",
      "sourceId": "8037",
      "title": "Roll Analyzer",
      "previous": {
        "modVersion": "0.2.2",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.4.1.0",
        "fileName": "wot_roll_analyzer_0.2.2.zip",
        "updatedAt": "2026-10-19T10:58:32.456Z",
        "changeLog": ""
      },
      "current": {
        "modVersion": "0.2.11",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.4.1.0",
        "fileName": "wot_roll_analyzer_0.2.11.zip",
        "updatedAt": "2026-10-20T14:26:26.832Z",
        "changeLog": "New\n- Settings window: set your own thresholds for when a row's roll turns green (in your favour) or red (against you), 1–25% each, with − / + buttons. Default is still 10%; the battle summary is coloured as before.\n\nChanged\n- Row colour follows the shown percentage: \"+10%\" at a 10% threshold is always green (it could stay white at 9.96%).\n\nFixed\n- The native damage log comes back if our panel stops updating due to an error or breaks in the first seconds of battle.\n- If the game didn't report a battle's end, the next battle closes the previous one properly.\n- On unload, the mod restores the native log without touching other mods' changes.\n- A hit you survived before the fatal one is no longer marked as a finishing blow.\n- Post-battle notification: consistent rounding; vehicles without mechanics show a normal summary.\n- Log rows no longer jump into the summary row if it failed to draw; assist rows stay even if the assist type is unknown."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "added",
